  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the most probable outcomes (in terms of value and probability), and prefers the lottery with the more favorable most probable outcome. In both lotteries, the most probable outcome is 0 Euros. Since both have the same most probable outcome (0), and 0 is not favorable, the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not consider the most probable outcome at all — instead, they focus on the chance of getting a positive outcome (i.e., avoiding zero). This reflects a different decision criterion (preference for positive outcomes or non-zero gains), not the evaluation of the most probable outcome. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The information considered (chance of winning something positive) is not relevant to the most probable outcome. The justification (preference for a chance to win something) does not follow the rule of comparing the most probable outcomes. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
